.TH P3M-RM 1 "@DATE@" "p3m @VERSION@" "p3m Manual"
.SH NAME
p3m-rm \- parallel recursive remove with a hard root guard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B p3m-rm
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR PATH | MASK ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B p3m-rm
removes files and directory trees using a pool of worker threads, like
.BR "rm \-rf" .
Arguments are literal paths or glob masks (expanded with
.BR glob (3));
quote masks to stop the shell expanding them, for example
.BR "p3m\-rm '/data/tmp\-*'" .
.PP
Without
.B \-\-apply
this is a
.B dry run
that only lists, as CSV, everything that would be removed.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-apply ,
the parallel walk unlinks files as it scans and collects directories, which
are then removed deepest level first so that parents never race their
children.
A missing entry is treated as already removed, as with
.BR "rm \-f" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Actually remove (the default is a dry run).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fIN\fR"
Worker threads (default: the number of online CPUs).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the CSV to
.I FILE
and show a live progress display.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the console listing; progress and the summary are still shown, and a
.B \-o
file is still written.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH SAFETY
.IP \(bu 2
Any path that resolves to
.B /
is refused outright, before any work starts, and aborts the whole run.
This guard cannot be overridden.
.B .
and
.B ..
are refused as well.
.IP \(bu 2
Symbolic links are never followed: the link itself is removed and its target
is untouched.
Every directory is opened with
.B O_NOFOLLOW
so a directory swapped for a symlink mid-run cannot redirect deletion.
.IP \(bu 2
The guard pass completes before the first entry is unlinked.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Errors were encountered.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or root-guard refusal.
.SH EXAMPLES
See what would be removed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-rm '/scratch/build\-*'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove it, showing only progress and the summary:
.PP
.RS
.nf
p3m\-rm \-\-apply \-q '/scratch/build\-*'
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p3m (7),
.BR p3m\-find (1),
.BR rm (1)
